==English==
{{wikipedia|anticlimax}}

===Etymology===
{{term|anti-}} + {{term|climax}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|anticlimaxes}}

# A [[failed]] or [[reverse]] [[climax]], ''[[particularly]]'':
## {{context|literature}} An [[unsatisfying]] [[resolution]] to a [[narrative]], [[usually]] [[owing to]] a ''[[deus ex machina]]'' or [[similarly]] [[trivial]] [[resolution]] of the [[main]] [[conflict]].
## {{context|rhetoric}} An [[abrupt]] [[descent]] ([[either]] [[deliberate]] or [[unintentional]]) from the [[dignity]] of the [[idea]] which the [[speaker]] or [[writer]] [[appear]]ed to be [[aiming]] for.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|partial}} [[bathos]]

====Antonyms====
